ity is term/state dependent: campaigns require promotability and no unapplied committed configuration changes, pre-campaign does not increment term, elections reset vote accounting, and becoming leader resets progress and appends an empty entry. Step filters older-term responses and normally relinquishes authority on higher terms, with explicit pre-vote and leader-lease exceptions. Thus old replication support is not simply carried into new leadership, whereas committed history and snapshot state survive authority changes. Async entry-stability responses carry the producing term; stale responses do not stabilize entries, but snapshot completion is still processed. A4 configuration changes replace the quorum context used by A1, and restored snapshots reconstruct membership. A5/A6 consumption crosses Ready/Advance or ordered local append/apply queues; the application owns actual durable writes and state-machine application. These are source observations and interface duties, not executed evidence.',remaining=['Complete the usable AuditSpec with exact producer/consumer relationships, election tally consumption, log commit term guard, timer/transfer paths, configuration validation and application boundaries.', 'Investigate the sourced continuation asymmetry: successful maybeCommit from append responses releases pendingReadIndexMessages, while successful maybeCommit from switchToConfig broadcasts append without that release. Determine whether legal application/election ordering can leave a pending read when this second path first commits a current-term entry; do not assume that history is reachable.', 'Trace reset and term transitions for pendingReadIndexMessages separately from the readOnly acknowledgment tracker, and establish caller completion/retry duties before asserting any read continuation obligation.', 'Reconcile README message-send ordering with the more specific Ready contract before constructing a synchronous persistence driver.'],rationale='The source establ